(Regression test: the runtime flag parser calls _str_eq to match
argument tokens against flag aliases, but the codegen did not mark
string.asm as needed. A program that declared and parsed flags yet used
no strings anywhere else (no string Print, no format strings) therefore
failed to assemble with "symbol `_str_eq' not defined". This program
parses flags and produces only numeric output, so string.asm is
required solely by the flag parser.)

a flag called "retries" is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number with default 3.
a flag called "verbose" is "-v" or "--verbose", it is a boolean.
Parse flags.

Set total to retries add 1.
Print total.
If verbose then, Print 1. Otherwise, Print 0.